title: help panel
tags: Panel [[In-app help]]
kind: reference
summary: Shows the documentation: a box to open a page by name or search all of them, and the page, with the keys read from your bindings.

Open it with <<key "help:open" "h h">> (`help:open`, optionally followed by what to
look for) or with `panel:open here help` (<<key "panel:open here help" "t h">>).
Without anything to look for, it shows the entry page ([[Documentation]]).

!! The box

The box at the top has the focus when the panel is shown; Enter leaves it (see Keys below).

* An ''exact name'' opens the page as soon as it is typed: a page's title or one of its other names, a command, a panel type ([[In-app help]]).
* Anything else searches every page, as you type, without regard to case: the pages whose title contains the text first, then those whose body does, each with the line around the first occurrence. Clicking a result opens the page.
* `#` in front searches even for an exact name.
* An empty box lists every page, by title.

The search leaves out the developer documentation unless ''include developer
documentation in the search'' is ticked. An exact name opens a developer page
regardless.

!! Keys

The box behaves like the query fields of the [[metarecord-list panel]]:

|<<key "help:apply search" Enter>> |search, and leave the box: the panel's keys work again |
|<<key "help:apply search stay" Shift+Enter>> |search, and stay in the box |
|<<key "help:clear search stay" c>> |empty the box |
|<<key "help:clear search" s>> |empty the box and go into it |
|<<key "help:focus search" "e s">> |go into the box, its text kept |
|<<key "help:back" Backspace>> |back to the page shown before, as in a browser; a search is not a step: back from one is the page it was typed over |
|<<key "help:forward" Shift+Backspace>> |forward again, after going back |
|<<key "cursor:parent self" Left>> |up to the page's topic — the page of its first tag ([[Generic panel commands]]) |
|<<key "help:open-hints" d>> |label the links in view with letters, to follow one (below) |

!! A page

Above a page are its topics, as buttons opening each topic's own page, and a badge
when the page is developer documentation or describes something that is not
implemented (`deferred`, `proposed`) or no longer current (`record`).

A link goes to another page. The keys are filled in from your bindings
([[In-app help]]). To search inside the page, use <<key "find:open" Ctrl+f>>
([[Find in a panel]]).

!! Following a link from the keyboard

<<key "help:open-hints" d>> puts a label of one or more letters on every link in
view — the topics above the page, the links in it, or the results of a search —
the way avy jumps in Emacs. Typing a label follows its link; while a label is half
typed, only the ones it starts are shown, and a letter no label continues is
ignored. Escape cancels and leaves the page as it was.

The letters go to a small box under the search box (`focus = "hints"`), so no other
key takes them while the labels are shown. Only what is in view is labelled, so the
labels stay short: one letter for up to 26 links, two beyond. To reach a link
further down, scroll to it first.

!! When the documentation is not installed

A bar says so and names the step that installs it; the panel has no page to show
until then. The documentation is installed with the rest of the configuration
([[Updating the configuration]]).
